# Numerical analysis in Litex: Newton's method for sqrt(2).
#
# newton_iteration.lit defines the iteration and its gap.
# gap_bound.lit proves that the gap is at most sqrt_two_newton_gap_bound(n).

iteration::newton_sqrt_two(1) = 3 / 2
iteration::newton_sqrt_two(3 / 2) = 17 / 12

by thm proof::sqrt_two_newton_gap_bound(2) => iteration::sqrt_two_newton_gap(2) <= iteration::sqrt_two_newton_gap_bound(2)
iteration::sqrt_two_newton_gap_bound(2) = 1 / 64
iteration::sqrt_two_newton_gap(2) <= 1 / 64
